        915.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Another type of controlled radical polymerization process was also reported by Ishihara.<sup>[19]</sup> Preparation of a high-density poly(MPC) brush has been reported by Iwasaki<sup>[20]</sup> and $\\mathrm { B r a s h } ^ { [ 2 1 ] }$using surface-initiated ATRP from a silicon substrate, immobilized 2-bromoisobutylate group.",
      "evidence_id": "ev001"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_3_40",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        89.0,
        569.0,
        486.0,
        915.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Similarly, the graft density of the poly(DMAEMA) brush was determined to be 0.40 chains/nm<sup>2</sup>.",
      "evidence_id": "ev002"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_3_42",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        500.0,
        259.0,
        900.0,
        743.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The contact angle of the water droplet (2.0 mL) on the poly(MPC) brush surface was $1 \\sim 3 ^ { \\circ }$The contact angle against methylene iodide and hexadecane were $4 5 ^ { \\circ }$and ${ < } 5 ^ { \\circ }$, respectively.",
      "evidence_id": "ev003"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_3_42",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        500.0,
        259.0,
        900.0,
        743.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The contact angle of the poly(DMAEMA) brush was reduced from $5 6 ^ { \\circ }$to $3 6 ^ { \\circ }$by immersion in methyl iodide solution, indicating the formation of a hydrophilic poly(METAI) brush.",
      "evidence_id": "ev004"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_3_44",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        500.0,
        792.0,
        898.0,
        915.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Figure 1(a) and (b) shows the NR profile and corresponding scattering density of a poly(METAI) brush at the D<sub>2</sub>O/Poly(ME-TAI) and 1.0 M NaCl/poly(METAI) interface.",
      "evidence_id": "ev005"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "T_4_49",
      "page": 4,
      "bbox": [
        96.0,
        67.0,
        903.0,
        217.0
      ],
      "source_type": "table",
      "source_sentence": "poly(MPC)",
      "evidence_id": "ev006"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "T_4_49",
      "page": 4,
      "bbox": [
        96.0,
        67.0,
        903.0,
        217.0
      ],
      "source_type": "table",
      "source_sentence": "poly(DMAEMA)",
      "evidence_id": "ev007"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "T_4_49",
      "page": 4,
      "bbox": [
        96.0,
        67.0,
        903.0,
        217.0
      ],
      "source_type": "table",
      "source_sentence": "poly(METAI)",
      "evidence_id": "ev008"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_4_56",
      "page": 4,
      "bbox": [
        96.0,
        328.0,
        493.0,
        537.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The scattering length density profiles of the poly(MPC) brushes in $\\mathbf { D } _ { 2 } \\mathbf { O }$calculated from the reflectivity curves indicated that the poly(METAI) chains were stretched up to 60 nm in $\\mathbf { D } _ { 2 } \\mathbf { O } _ { 3 }$, forming a concentration gradient of ${ \\bf D } _ { 2 } { \\bf O } .$.",
      "evidence_id": "ev009"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_4_56",
      "page": 4,
      "bbox": [
        96.0,
        328.0,
        493.0,
        537.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "For instance, assuming the swollen brush thickness was 60 nm, the $M _ { \\mathrm { n } }$was 126,000, and grafting density was 0.40 chains/nm<sup>2</sup>, the ionic concentration in swollen poly (METAI) brush layer can be estimated to be 4.2 M, which is much higher than salt concentration in aqueous solution.",
      "evidence_id": "ev010"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_5_69",
      "page": 5,
      "bbox": [
        89.0,
        466.0,
        486.0,
        675.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Negligible change was also observed betweenthe swellingstructureofpoly(MPC) facing a pure $\\mathbf { D } _ { 2 } \\mathbf { O }$and a NaCl deuterium oxide solution, as shown in Figure 1 (c) and (d).",
      "evidence_id": "ev011"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_5_69",
      "page": 5,
      "bbox": [
        89.0,
        466.0,
        486.0,
        675.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "We found that the dimension of free poly(MPC) in water is independent of the ionic strength of the salt solution.<sup>[25,26]</sup> Poly(MPC) can be regard as a quite unique zwitter-type polyelectrolyte having the independence of intra- and intermolecular interaction of PMPC from the concentration of $\\mathrm { N a C l } .",
      "evidence_id": "ev012"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_5_73",
      "page": 5,
      "bbox": [
        500.0,
        363.0,
        898.0,
        675.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Figure 2 shows the friction coefficient of poly(MPC) and poly(METAI) brush surfaces measured using a sliding a glass ball in air and in water at 298 K.",
      "evidence_id": "ev013"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_6_82",
      "page": 6,
      "bbox": [
        96.0,
        603.0,
        493.0,
        915.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The salt concentration effect on the polyelectrolyte brush has attracted much attention due to increased understanding of the molecular interactions and dispersion of brush grafted nanoparticles in aqueous media.<sup>[28]</sup> Figure 3(a) and (b) show the friction coefficient of poly(MPC) and poly(METAI) brushes in 0 \u0003 1.0 M of NaCl solution, respectively.",
      "evidence_id": "ev014"
    },
    {
